  $ym$E-commerce Main Image - Pale Silver-Gray Corset and Maxi Skirt$ym$, $ym$E-commerce Main Image - Pale Silver-Gray Corset and Maxi Skirt$ym$, $ym$A highly detailed wardrobe prompt for a silver-gray and white corset top paired with an off-white floral maxi skirt.$ym$, $ym$A highly detailed wardrobe prompt for a silver-gray and white corset top paired with an off-white floral maxi skirt.$ym$,
  $ym$PROTECTED WARDROBE RULE — HIGHEST PRIORITY: Treat each garment description below as its immutable final product identity. Preserve construction, parts, hardware, material, pattern, and every registered graphic or marking—its surface, side, orientation, scale, colors, content, spelling, and count. FINAL WORN STATE overrides only the scoped item's use, position, side, orientation, fastening, layering, folds, tucks, knots, and drape. A SOURCE GARMENT label describes the unstyled item, never the completed silhouette. Do not redesign, add, remove, mirror, duplicate, relocate, or redraw protected details. Wardrobe: Top: One pale silver-gray and white strapless overbust corset top made from medium-weight structured woven corsetry fabric with a fine diagonal surface, low sheen, firm shape retention, and slim vertical boning channels. The close longline silhouette ends at the upper hip, narrowing through the waist before opening slightly over the lower side panels. A pronounced sweetheart upper edge shapes two curved bust cups around a shallow center notch, with scalloped white floral lace and fine eyelash fringe tracing the complete upper perimeter. Curved cup seams, princess seams, and narrow boning channels divide the front, side, and rear into tapered panels; a white bound edge follows the complete lower contour. White lace forms an all-over botanical field of large blossoms, small rosettes, leafy stems, curling vines, and open net regions across the pale front, both sides, and rear panels, with denser scalloped motifs along the bust edge. A vertical champagne gold corset busk closes the center front. Two white center-rear plackets carry parallel rows of antique-gold-tone grommets, crossed by one wide white satin ribbon from the straight rear upper edge to the lower edge and finished in a secure tied closure. Keep the lace edges crisp against the pale base, the boning channels narrow and straight, the busk and grommets firmly seated, and the ribbon broad and flat through every crossing. Bottom: One off-white ankle-length tiered maxi skirt made from lightweight semi-sheer floral voile, white Swiss-dot dobby voile, and broad white floral mesh lace. It has a full softly flared A-line silhouette with a narrow upper contour and a wide flowing lower sweep. A narrow waistband forms the level upper opening. The main upper panel extends from the waistband to the lower calf and joins one broad gathered Swiss-dot lower tier through a level horizontal seam. Tiny coral-pink floral sprigs with faint pale-sage foliage scatter evenly across the upper panel; narrow scalloped white trim follows the tier join, and tiny raised dots cover the lower tier. A wide open floral-lace border overlays the lower portion of the dotted tier, with a wavy scalloped upper boundary, linked blossoms and leaves across fine mesh, and a deep scalloped outer hem. Concealed elastic within the waistband provides a clean pull-on closure. The rear repeats the floral field, the level gathered join, the dotted tier, and the overlaid lace border around the full circumference. Keep the voile airy and softly draped, the printed sprigs delicate and distinct, the raised dots regular, and the lace open and finely resolved. Footwear: One matching pair of champagne-gold open-toe stiletto sandals, identical except for anatomical mirroring. Each shoe has a slim rounded forefoot strap, a second fine diagonal strap crossing the instep, and a narrow slingback circuit completed by a concealed elastic join at the rear. The upper straps are smooth low-luster leather-like material with fine folded edges and minimal seam bulk. A thin champagne insole follows a narrow tapered footbed above a very shallow outsole, ending in a slender medium-height stiletto heel with a straight shaft and a compact heel tip. Keep both shoes equal in strap width, strap route, toe opening, heel height, color, section thickness, and finish. Necklace: One short delicate pale-gold necklace made from a very fine oval-link chain with an even slender section and soft warm polish. The continuous circuit consists of repeating small links, carries no pendant or station ornament, and closes with one compact spring-ring clasp and a matching terminal ring. Keep the link joins crisp enough to remain visible without increasing the chain's fine scale. Earrings: One matching pair of small polished gold-tone sculptural post-drop earrings. Each member combines a short slim top stem with one thick rounded metal bar that curves into an irregular elongated teardrop outline, narrows toward the top, and curls inward at the lower interior before returning upward, leaving a clearly open center. The pair has identical contour, scale, section thickness, and reflective finish. Low-profile posts and compact backs complete both members. Keep the rounded bar continuous, the inward curls crisp, the open centers unobstructed, and the polished reflections controlled along the curved sections. Bracelet: One broad champagne gold beaded bracelet constructed as a single flexible multi-row circuit from several closely packed parallel strands. The strands alternate large polished champagne gold round beads, smaller pale round beads, and clear faceted beads, interlaced into one dense band with controlled spacing and a softly articulated section. Concealed elastic cords close the circuit without exposed hardware. Keep the bead-size hierarchy distinct, the rows parallel through the full circumference, and the reflective metal, pale beads, and clear facets cleanly separated. Final worn state: VIEW-CONDITIONAL BODY-SIDE MAP: front view — wearer-left is image-right and wearer-right is image-left; back view — wearer-left is image-left and wearer-right is image-right. In profiles, crossed limbs, or ambiguity, trace the named anatomical side continuously from its corresponding shoulder, hip, eye, or ear landmark as applicable. Apply the state only to the named anatomical side; never mirror, swap, or duplicate it. - Bracelet placement: Render one complete instance of the registered bracelet from the item description immediately above around only the wearer-left wrist. Keep the wearer-right wrist free of this bracelet; do not mirror or duplicate it. Preserve the registered design and count. Keep other separately selected wrist items unchanged.$ym$, $ym$PROTECTED WARDROBE RULE — HIGHEST PRIORITY: Treat each garment description below as its immutable final product identity. Preserve construction, parts, hardware, material, pattern, and every registered graphic or marking—its surface, side, orientation, scale, colors, content, spelling, and count. FINAL WORN STATE overrides only the scoped item's use, position, side, orientation, fastening, layering, folds, tucks, knots, and drape. A SOURCE GARMENT label describes the unstyled item, never the completed silhouette. Do not redesign, add, remove, mirror, duplicate, relocate, or redraw protected details. Wardrobe: Top: One pale silver-gray and white strapless overbust corset top made from medium-weight structured woven corsetry fabric with a fine diagonal surface, low sheen, firm shape retention, and slim vertical boning channels. The close longline silhouette ends at the upper hip, narrowing through the waist before opening slightly over the lower side panels. A pronounced sweetheart upper edge shapes two curved bust cups around a shallow center notch, with scalloped white floral lace and fine eyelash fringe tracing the complete upper perimeter. Curved cup seams, princess seams, and narrow boning channels divide the front, side, and rear into tapered panels; a white bound edge follows the complete lower contour. White lace forms an all-over botanical field of large blossoms, small rosettes, leafy stems, curling vines, and open net regions across the pale front, both sides, and rear panels, with denser scalloped motifs along the bust edge. A vertical champagne gold corset busk closes the center front. Two white center-rear plackets carry pa